+Hardware support scaffolding for Aegis
+
+This directory contains templates, Dockerfile examples, device-plugin manifests, nodepool provisioning helpers,
+backend adapter scaffolds and runbooks to integrate the following accelerators into Aegis:
+ - NVIDIA GPUs (CUDA) — fully scaffolded; requires CUDA drivers on nodes and validated container images.
+ - Cloud TPUs (GCP) — TPU VM/operator guidance and TPU-backed backend using JAX/libtpu (placeholder).
+ - AWS Inferentia / Trainium — device-plugin/Neuron runtime template and backend adapter stub.
+ - Graphcore IPU — Poplar/Graphcore SDK device-plugin template and backend adapter stub.
+ - Habana Gaudi — Habana device-plugin/HCX SDK template and backend adapter stub.
+ - Generic Edge NPU (Coral/EdgeTPU or vendor NPUs) — generic device-plugin template and backend adapter stub.
+
+Notes:
+ - All Dockerfiles are templates and must be built on infrastructure that has access to the vendor toolchains and drivers.
+ - Device-plugin manifests are provider/operator templates (tweak images/versions and RBAC to your environment).
+ - Backend adapters are implemented as best-effort async wrappers that call vendor runtimes where available,
+   and otherwise fall back to the HF/vLLM reference implementation.
+ - Use the provided runbooks to install device plugins and validate workloads in a staging environment.
+
