+# Hardware validation & perf tuning runbook
+
+1. Build or pull the appropriate hardware image (see ops/hw/dockerfiles).
+2. Deploy the image to a single-node test pool of the target hardware.
+3. Start the async batched inference server on the node.
+4. Run ops/ci/load_test_async.py with INFERENCE_TARGET set to the service and measure p50/p95/p99.
+5. Use ops/ci/backpressure_probe.py to check time-to-first-token under burst load.
+6. Tune BATCH_MAX_SIZE and BATCH_TIMEOUT_SEC based on latency vs throughput tradeoffs.
+7. For GPUs, validate GPU memory utilization (nvidia-smi). For TPUs, validate host-side compile times and device utilization.
